; game.xon -- the kettle set: the valley above the Delve, a world of
; screens, and no descent.
;
; What this set turns on: a world of screens, (world screens W H),
; joined at their edges and kept, with the door into Kettle, the town,
; on the hub screen in the middle; open ground, (level-style open),
; with (clumps LO HI) thickets over (clump-size LO HI) square metres;
; sight to eight; hunger as a store; the rings out from the town as
; bands, each laying its caches.
; A screen's depth is its distance from the hub, so what lives on it,
; and the gold on it, grow with the walk out.  The goal is in someone's
; keeping, at the end of a chain of trades drawn each game from
; scenes.xon, and bringing it back to Kettle's square is the win.

(set "kettle")
(title "Kettle")

(world screens 7 5)

; The valley is drawn at 21, a cell 21 metres across and 34 down, a
; screen some 1700 metres by 750; the town's ground stands on the hub
; at its own size, a block of 23 cells by 6 (see interiors.x).
(scale 21)

; The town is the set beside this one, a region of the same world: its
; door is on the hub (see interiors.xon), and the game starts through
; it, on the square, (start NAME) naming the door.  The Delve lies under
; the town, gone into from its pithead.
(join "town")
(start "Kettle")

; The goal: its name and its glyph; with no level it lies nowhere, and
; is given by the last link of the chain (see scenes.xon).  (chain LO
; HI) is how many links a chain has at most.
(goal "the Guild ledger" "*")
(chain 2 3)

; What a game is worth: the gold, each errand run, each screen walked
; and each door gone through, and the ledger brought home.
(score (gold 1) (quests 100) (screens 10) (places 25) (won 1000))

; What a thing is worth in gold at a counter, by its class; an item's own
; (price N) is in front of this.  A shop asks and pays its (rate SELL
; BUY) percent of it (shops.x).
(worth (potion 12) (scroll 14) (wand 40) (ring 50) (weapon 16) (armour 20) (food 4) (oil 5))

(player 14 16)
(unarmed 1 3)

; Food in seconds, a turn the time to walk a cell: half a day's at the
; start; felt with four hours left, weakening with one; a day's the
; most.  Past nothing, (starve N) costs a hit point every N seconds.
(hunger 43200 14400 3600 86400)
(starve 600)

; Sight to eight cells, through nothing solid.
(view 8)

; Open ground: thickets of wall, the outer ring always clear.
(level-style open)
(clumps 8 14)
(clump-size 11000 34000)

; The valley's ground in metres: the closes, (close W H), and the
; road's gates, (gate-first LO HI) in and (gate-gap LO HI) apart, and
; of the ways made through a close's shut sides (gaps PERCENT) gaps; the
; hills' edges, (edge-length LO HI), the boulders (boulder-drop LO HI)
; below them, and bog and gorse in square metres, (bog-size LO HI) and
; (gorse-size LO HI); the rim's scars, (scar-across LO HI) along and
; (scar-down LO HI) down, its ruins (ruin-width LO HI) by (ruin-depth
; LO HI), and its standing stones (stone-gap M) apart.
(close 210 136)
(gate-first 63 252)
(gate-gap 210 504)
(gaps 35)
(edge-length 420 1050)
(boulder-drop 68 102)
(bog-size 14000 43000)
(gorse-size 5700 14000)
(scar-across 315 840)
(scar-down 170 408)
(ruin-width 126 294)
